ly gained any  useful skills  um and i'm also a bad liar you know a  good actor is very different than a liar  and it's it's two different things so i  have that same problem i guess it's for  the better though  it is i think yeah the obligatory  westworld question for you  yes i know with some shows it can take a  little bit of time  to kind of get in the groove and you  find that groove  in seasons one and two and then they  kind of completely  shake up the show in season three so did  you have that period at the beginning  of the season where you felt yourself  readjusting  even to a show you knew so well  absolutely  it's not like that every season a bit  season three for sure because that was  just shooting a completely  different show um but luckily it's still  the same people  every year it's the same the same crew  that's been with us since the beginning  um and so it now we've been doing it so  long it very much is like a family  and it's still you know even though the  seasons change  it's still just as chaotic behind the  scenes and so it there's something  comforting about that  because it doesn't change um  but every season is is a reinvention and  jonah made that very clear  um from the beginning that you know  tear down the sets after every season  and start again  and and it's bittersweet because you get  to know these characters really well and  you like them how they are and then you  have to kind of start over every season  but i think it's what keeps it  interesting  that's what makes me excited for future  seasons so yeah what's season four going  to be  even i don't know  right now yeah no one's gonna forget but  also huge congratulations on this  i really i really really love this one  it's a it's a special one and  i wouldn't expect any less from you guys  miranda so huge congratulations  thank you so much i feel the same way

